' =====================================================================
' RoboFetch - A6: the four physical gates PASS and the classifier
' refuses. The counterpart to scenario 2, where the physics refused and
' the model was never reached.
'
' Figures are real: SKU-2001 (3.2 kg) from a 74% battery leaves 15.8%,
' which clears the 15% reserve - and the model still calls it
' infeasible at 67% confidence. Verified by running the exported model.
' =====================================================================
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #34495E
  LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
  ParticipantBorderColor #34495E
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FBFCFE
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #EAF2FA
}

actor Controller as C
participant "Web tier" as API
database "SQLite" as DB
participant "AI service" as AI
participant "Task manager" as TM

== Cost the job ==
C -> API ++ : POST /preview  SKU-2001 -> delivery_1
API -> DB ++ : product, pick point, bay
DB --> API -- : 3.2 kg, pick (1.05, 0.95), bay (-3.0, -2.2)
API -> DB ++ : live robot condition
DB --> API -- : battery 74%, 30 C, condition 100%
API -> API : project, then cost the three legs

== The physics allows it ==
API -> API : gate 1  stock: passes
API -> API : gate 2  reserve: leaves 15.8%,\nclears the 15% minimum
API -> API : gate 3  thermal: peak 57.6 C,\nunder the 70 C limit
API -> API : gate 4  condition: 100%, above 30%

== Only now is the model asked ==
API -> AI ++ : predict  battery 74%, 3.2 kg, 11.4 m
AI --> API -- : infeasible, confidence 67%
API --> C -- : REFUSED  decided_by = model\n"predicted infeasible in the robot's\ncurrent condition (confidence 67%)"

note over API, TM
  The order is affordable, cool enough and the robot is healthy, so the
  physics would have accepted it. The model refuses because 15.8% is a
  hair above the 15% line and it was trained on jittered thresholds.
  Nothing is written and the task manager is never told.
end note

@enduml
